\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Away, my needless fears,
\par And doubts no longer minne;
\par A messenger divine.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Thrice comfortable hope,
\par That calms my troubled breast;
\par My father's hand prepares the cup,
\par And what he wills is the best.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. If what I wish is good,
\par And suits the will divine;
\par By earth and hell in vain withstood,
\par I know it shall be mine.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Still let them counsel take
\par To frustrate his decree,
\par They cannot keep a blessing back
\par By heaven designed for me.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Here then I doubt no more,
\par But in His pleasure rest,
\par Whose wisdom, love, and thruth, and power
\par Engage to make me blest.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. To accomplish His design
\par The creatures all agree;
\par And all the attributes divine
\par Are now at work for me.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

